            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Mary flips a coin, rolls a six-sided die and draws a card from a deck of 52 playing cards. Find the probability that she got tails, an even number, and a black card.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{8}$",
      "worked": "The three stages are independent. There are three even die outcomes and 26 black cards.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{tails, even and black})&=\\frac{1}{2}\\times\\frac{3}{6}\\times\\frac{26}{52}\\\\P(\\text{tails, even and black})&=\\frac{1}{8}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
